  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO World Water Assessment Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UNESCO World Water Assessment Programme assesses and reports on freshwater issues to provide responses, develop case studies, enhance assessment capacities at a national and regional levels, and inform decision-making processes. WWAP makes available to decision-makers, inside and outside the water box, data, indicators, background information and projections about the state, use and management of water resources. This is accomplished through the production of the annual WWDRs; outreach and advocacy activities; capacity development programmes; projects on water assessments, water and gender, and emerging fields.</narrative>
  </description>
